\**{c=red:Note:}** This Mission is essentially identical for all 3 {z:Nations}. While each {z:Nations} requires you to travel to the other two, they all follow the same path.
:* {p:San d'Orians|San d'Oria} and {p:Windurstians|Windurst} who choose {p:Bastok} first will do the same things. Therefore, it IS possible to group people together from different {z:Nations} to ultimately end up on the same BCNM fight.
:* A {p:Windurstian|Windurst} may choose to do the {p:Bastok} portion first, and {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion second, while a {p:Bastokan|Bastok} can do the {p:Windurstian|Windurst} portion first, and the {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion second. In this scenario, {p:Windurstians|Windurst} and {p:Bastokans|Bastok} can enter the same BCNM for the {p:San d'Orian|San d'Oria} portion.
:* Players who have already completed this Mission (for any {z:Nation}) may enter any of the BC, except for the one associated with their Nation.

::* E.g. A {p:Windurstian|Windurst} who has completed 2-3 is unable to enter the Giddeus BCNM to help others, unless they have completed this battle through another Nation's 2-3 Mission.

=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough Crystals (3+) to a {p:Conquest Overseer} if you wish to skip Mission 2-2 and immediately unlock this one, then accept it from the Gate Guard.
* You will be instructed to speak with {p:Halver}. He is located at (I-9) just inside the door of {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}, entered from {z:Northern San d'Oria}.
* {p:Halver} will instruct you to visit two other Nations: {p:Bastok} and {p:Windurst}.
** After reaching {M:Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|The Path Untraveled} you will be given a {i:Cipher: Halver|Cipher: Halver|10158} if you do not already possess this Trust.
* The next leg of this Mission can be done in two different ways:
** Go to {p:Bastok} first and then to {p:Windurst}.
** Go to {p:Windurst} first and then {p:Bastok}.
* If you have never visited {p:Bastok} or {p:Windurst}, you can "Unity warp" to either {z:South Gustaberg} or {z:East Sarutabaruta}, then make the rest of the trek on foot. Speak to {n:Urbiolaine} in Southern San d'Oria (G-10) and choose "Bring me to a {p:Wanted encounter area|Category:Unity Concord}", then "Content level 99 and below."
* The **Bastok Path** may be quicker due to the ease of obtaining the item involved.
** Bastok will require obtaining a {@i:Mine Gravel|597} {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597}, which can be bought off the Auction House.
** Windurst will require obtaining two {@i:Parana Shield|12298} {i:Parana Shields|Parana Shield|12298}, but these are 100% drops and can be obtained in 5 minutes apart.
* The **Windurst Path** final BCNM may be a bit easier as the {p:Petrify} AoE will not be used.

=2 Option 1: Bastok Path
=3 San d'Oria to Bastok
* Once you get to {p:Bastok} head to the {z:Metalworks} and speak with {n:Savae E Paleade} at the **San d'Orian Consulate** located on the top floor at (I-9).
* Next speak with {n:Pius} inside the **Dept. of Industry** located on the same floor of the {z:Metalworks} at (J-8).
* You will be asked to speak to {n:Grohm}. He is inside the **Craftsmen's Eatery** at (G-9) of the top floor and gives you 3 {i:Pickaxes|Pickaxe|605} when you talk to him.
** In the unlikely event that you already have a {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599} sitting around, you can now use it right away by trading it to {n:Savae E Paleade} and be able to skip to the last step in this section.
*** Since the item has the 'Alt' (CanSendPOL) tag, an extra from another character within the same PlayOnline account can transfer them to other characters. However, since it's {E} it can't be traded between characters otherwise.
*** You also might have one from {M:Windurst Mission 2-3|Windurst Mission 2-3|The Three Kingdoms} or by simply already exploring the mines. /itemsearch "Mythril Sand" can help you find any onzes you might already have.
* Your main task now is to acquire one {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599}:
** At this point you should head to the {z:Auction House} and buy one {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} (Others > Misc. 1) to save a lot of time and walking. If you do not want to do this and want to do the work yourself, use the 3 {i:Pickaxes|Pickaxe|605} you are given during the cutscene (you are __not__ guaranteed to mine the gravel with only 3 axes used).
** You can also buy {i:Pickaxes|Pickaxe|605} from {n:Boytz} at (H-7) of {z:Bastok Mines} or {n:Numa} at (E-7) of {z:Port Bastok} if you feel the need to mine it yourself, or if the AH does not have sufficient supply.
** A map of {z:Palborough Mines} can be purchased for 600 Gil from {n:Karine} at (H-9) of {z:Bastok Markets} or {n:Rex} at (J-7) of {z:Port Bastok}.
* Head to {z:Palborough Mines}, enter at (K-3) of {z:North Gustaberg}.
** The fastest way here initially (for character who has reached level 99), is to use {n:Domenic} to warp to {z:Waughroon Shrine}, then exit to the {z:Palborough Mines} Home Point. If the player uses /BLM, they can {s:Escape} to the entrance proper.
*** If you already have {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597}, you can go directly from the Home Point to the Refiner Lid.
** If you did not purchase the {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} at the {z:Auction House} follow the left wall until you get to (F-7). Look for a **Mythril Seam**. Trade your {i:Pickaxe|Pickaxe|605} to the seam until you get a {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597}.
*** There are also two **Mythril Seam**s on the west bank (in the northwest corner) of the room at I-8 on the way to the elevator.
* Once you have a {i:Mine Gravel|Mine Gravel|597} make your way to the **elevator** at (I-8) on the east bank and ride it up to the 3rd floor. The route there goes through the southern loop at (H-9).
** Make your way to Map 3's (I-6) where you will find a Refiner Lid. Trade our gravel to the Refiner Lid and then pull the Refiner Lever.
** Walk off the ledge or follow the path to the floor below and the bottom of the machine. Pull the Refiner Lever here and you will receive an Onz of {i:Mythril Sand|Mythril Sand|599}.
*** If you're doing the {p:Mythril Marathon|Category:Records of Eminence} RoE, you can trade in two batches and get all 10 at once at the bottom.
*** If you forgot to pull the lever at the top after trading, fear not: just run around the short loop to the southwest and the tunnel will ramp back up to the top.
* Return to the Consulate and trade the sand to {n:Savae E Paleade}. You can now head to {p:Windurst}.

=3 Bastok to Windurst
* First head to the **San d'Orian Consulate** in {z:Windurst Woods}, located at (F/G-10).
* Inside speak with {n:Mourices}. Then head to {z:Heavens Tower}. The entrance is at (H-7) of {z:Windurst Walls}.
* Inside speak with {n:Kupipi} for the {@k} {k:Dark key}. She is at the desk.
** After reaching {M:Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|The Path Untraveled} you will be given a {i:Cipher: Semih|Cipher: Semih|10157} if you do not already possess this Trust.
* Travel to {z:Giddeus}. The entrance is at (F-8) of {z:West Sarutabaruta}.
** A map of {z:Giddeus} can be purchased for 600 Gil from {n:Mhoji Roccoruhat|Mhoji Roccoruh} (G-9) of {z:Port Windurst} or {n:Pehki Machumaht} at (H-11) of {z:Windurst Woods}.
** Home Point #1 will take you right to the entrance of the BCNM, if you have it.
* Once inside {z:Giddeus} make your way to (F-12) and zone into {z:Balga's Dais}.
** This is an uncapped {p:BCNM} fight and {p:Trusts} can be used.
** All buffs besides food will be erased when you enter.
** Inside you will fight {m:Searcher} and {m:Black Dragon}.
** {m:Searcher}, {p:Ahriman} type monster.
*** Will cast {s:Black Magic} Spells including {p:Silence}.
** {m:Black Dragon}, {p:Dragon|Category:Dragon} type NM.
*** Will use an AoE attack that will cause {s:Poison} at 10 Hp per tick. Antidotes are recommended.
** Parties should {p:Elemental Seal} {s:Sleep} the {m:Black Dragon} and kill the {m:Searcher}. After the {m:Searcher} is dead the dragon should go down easily.
* After you will receive a cutscene and the {@k} {k:Kindred crest}.
** Optionally, you can speak with {n:Kupipi} in {z:Heavens Tower} again for a message afterwards.
* Speak with {n:Mourices} at the San d'Orian Consulate again for a cutscene and the {@k} {k:Kindred report}.
* Next return to San d'Oria and speak with {p:Halver} in {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}.

You will receive Rank 3, 3000 {p:Gil}, and a {@k} {k:Adventurer's Certificate}.
=2 Option 2: Windurst Path
=3 San d'Oria to Windurst
* First head to the **San d'Orian Consulate** in {z:Windurst Woods} (F/G-10).
* Inside speak with {n:Mourices}. Then head to {z:Heavens Tower}. The entrance is at (H-7) of {z:Windurst Walls}.
* Inside speak with {n:Kupipi} for the {@k} {k:Shield offering}. She is at the desk.
** After reaching {M:Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 1-7|The Path Untraveled} you will be given a {i:Cipher: Semih|Cipher: Semih|10157} if you do not already possess this Trust.
* You will now have to travel to {z:Giddeus}. The entrance is at (F-8) of {z:West Sarutabaruta}.
** A map of {z:Giddeus} can be purchased for 600 Gil from {n:Mhoji Roccoruh} at (G-9) of {z:Port Windurst} or {n:Pehki Machumaht} at (H-11) of {z:Windurst Woods}.
* Once inside, go to (G-8) and drop down the hole. Then head north to (G/H-7) and kill {m:Zhuu Buxu the Silent}.
** {m:Zhuu Buxu the Silent} is a {p:NIN} type {p:NM}. He will drop the {@i:Parana Shield|12298} {i:Parana Shield|Parana Shield|12298}.
** You will need 2 of these shields. Kill the NM once, wait for repop, then kill a second time. Repop is around 5 minutes.
* Now head west to (F-7). Speak with {n:Uu Zhoumo} to offer up the {@k} {k:Shield offering}.
* Return to the **San d'Orian Consulate** in {z:Windurst Woods} and trade your 2 {@i:Parana Shield|12298} {i:Parana Shields|Parana Shield|12298} to {n:Mourices}. After this you are ready to head to {p:Bastok}.

=3 Windurst to Bastok
* Once you get to {p:Bastok} head to the top floor of {z:Metalworks} and speak with {n:Savae E Paleade} at the **San d'Orian Consulate** located at (I-9).
* Next speak with {n:Pius} inside the **Dept. of Industry** in the President's office located on the same floor of the {z:Metalworks} at (J-8).
* You will be asked to speak to {n:Grohm}. He is inside the **Craftsmen's Eatery** at (G-9) of the top floor.
** A map of {z:Palborough Mines} can be purchased for 600 Gil from {n:Karine} at (H-9) of {z:Bastok Markets} or {n:Rex} at (J-7) of {z:Port Bastok}.
* Head to {z:Palborough Mines}, the entrance is at (K-3) of {z:North Gustaberg}.
* Inside follow the right wall until you reach an **elevator** at (I-8). Take this elevator to the top floor. Make your way to the {z:Waughroon Shrine} entrance at (H-10) and prepare for battle.
** All buffs besides food will be erased when you enter.
** Inside you will fight {m:Seeker} and {m:Dark Dragon}.
** {m:Seeker}, {p:Ahriman} type monster.
*** Will cast {s:Black Magic} Spells including {p:Silence}.
** {m:Dark Dragon}, {p:Dragon|Category:Dragon} type NM.
*** Will use an AoE attack called Petro Eyes that will cause {p:Petrify}.
** Parties should {p:Elemental Seal} {s:Sleep} the {m:Dark Dragon} and kill the {m:Seeker}. After the {m:Seeker} is dead the dragon should go down easily.
* After the fight zone out of {z:Waughroon Shrine} then head to and take the boat located at H-8 on the North side of the river. The boat will bring you back to {z:Bastok Mines} via {z:Zeruhn Mines}.
** It is not necessary to take the boat.
* Speak with {n:Savae E Paleade} at the **San d'Orian Consulate** again to get the {@k} {k:Kindred report}.
* Return to San d'Oria and speak with {p:Halver} in {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}.

You will receive Rank 3, 3000 {p:Gil}, and an {@k} {k:Adventurer's Certificate}.
=2 Notes
* Windurst Dragon was easily solo'ed on a level 25 RDM with 4 trusts, though I did sleep the dragon. The sleep landed first try. The fight can go badly if you don't land the sleep quickly.
* Easily solo'd at 30BLM with four Trusts.
* The BCNM has been solo'd by a Mnk/War, Pld/War, or Drg/Whm with meds and skill.
* Can also be solo'd by a Thf/Nin with capped {p:Marksmanship}, {p:Sleep Bolts|Sleep Bolt}, {p:Bloody Bolts|Bloody Bolt}, and a few meds.
* Easily solo'd as a 99COR.

